        "rationale": "<strong>Anticoagulant Therapy:</strong> Dicoumarol (similar to Warfarin) is a Vitamin K antagonist that affects the extrinsic clotting pathway (Factors II, VII, IX, X). The specific test to evaluate the extrinsic pathway is the Prothrombin Time (PT), often reported as an INR. <em>Note: While 'clotting time' is vague, PT is the medical standard for this medication.</em>",
        "type": "dental-deck"
