        "rawOptions": "a. Charged coupled device (CCD)<br>b. Intensifying screen phosphor (ISP)<br>c. Photostimulable phosphor (PSP)<br>d. ALARA",
        "answer": "a. Charged coupled device (CCD)",
        "rationale": "<strong>Sensors:</strong> The CCD (along with CMOS sensors) is the foundational solid-state silicon chip technology used in almost all direct-wired digital intraoral sensors today. It captures x-ray energy and instantly translates it into a digital image.",
