        "rawOptions": "a. Injury to the PSAN<br>b. Infection<br>c. Oroantral fistula formation<br>d. Poor access",
        "answer": "c. Oroantral fistula formation",
        "rationale": "<strong>Anatomy Risks:</strong> The maxillary sinus pneumatizes (expands) downwards as people age, particularly after posterior teeth are lost. Because the bony floor of the sinus dips directly into the tuberosity, surgical reduction risks perforating the bone and creating an opening into the sinus.",
        "type": "dental-deck"
