        "answer": "c. It will cause further distortion of the specimen",
        "rationale": "<strong>Biopsy Principles:</strong> Injecting fluid directly into the lesion artificially balloons and distorts the cellular architecture. This artifact makes it incredibly difficult for the oral pathologist to accurately evaluate the tissue under a microscope. Always use regional blocks or inject circumferentially around the lesion.",
