        "front": "1. Which of the following permanent teeth typically features a prominent mesial concavity extending from the cervical third of the crown down onto the root, making it highly susceptible to perforation during root canal therapy?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Maxillary first premolar</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Maxillary second premolar</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Mandibular first premolar</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Mandibular first molar</div></div>",
