        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "1. During the embryonic development of the face and oral cavity, the first branchial (pharyngeal) arch gives rise to which of the following structures?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The muscles of facial expression and the facial nerve.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Meckel's cartilage, the mandible, the maxilla, and the muscles of mastication.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Reichert's cartilage, the stapes, and the stylohyoid ligament.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The thymus gland and the inferior parathyroid glands.</div></div>",
