        "deckName": "Day 1 Block 2: Pathology, Micro, Embryo & Histology",
        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "2. In the Bell Stage of tooth development (morphodifferentiation), the enamel organ consists of four distinct layers. Which layer is primarily composed of glycosaminoglycans (GAGs) that draw in water, creating a star-shaped, cushioned network that protects the developing enamel?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Inner Enamel Epithelium</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Outer Enamel Epithelium</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Stratum Intermedium</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Stellate Reticulum</div></div>",
