        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "3. The dental papilla is a condensation of ectomesenchymal cells located directly beneath the enamel organ. The dental papilla is strictly responsible for forming which two tissues of the mature tooth?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Enamel and Dentin</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Dentin and Pulp</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Cementum and Periodontal Ligament</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Alveolar Bone and Cementum</div></div>",
