        "deckName": "Day 1 Block 2: Pathology, Micro, Embryo & Histology",
        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "6. Which of the following is considered the primary bacterial pathogen responsible for the INITIATION of dental caries on smooth enamel surfaces due to its ability to aggressively synthesize sticky extracellular glucans from sucrose?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Lactobacillus acidophilus</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Streptococcus mutans</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Actinomyces viscosus</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Porphyromonas gingivalis</div></div>",
