        "front": "9. To ensure proper sterilization and destruction of all highly resistant bacterial endospores, a standard gravity displacement steam autoclave must typically be operated at what parameters?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> 100°C (212°F) at 10 psi for 30 minutes</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> 121°C (250°F) at 15 psi for 15-20 minutes</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> 160°C (320°F) at 0 psi for 2 hours</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> 134°C (273°F) at 30 psi for 3 minutes</div></div>",
