        "front": "11. A 60-year-old male with a history of heavy smoking and alcohol abuse presents with a painless, indurated (firm), non-healing ulcer on the lateral border of his tongue. A biopsy confirms a malignant epithelial neoplasm. What is the most common form of oral cancer?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Basal Cell Carcinoma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Squamous Cell Carcinoma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Malignant Melanoma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Mucoepidermoid Carcinoma</div></div>",
