        "id": "deck-day1_block2-012",
        "deckId": "day1_block2",
        "deckName": "Day 1 Block 2: Pathology, Micro, Embryo & Histology",
        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "12. Radiographically, a benign but highly aggressive odontogenic tumor presents as a multilocular, \"soap bubble\" or \"honeycomb\" radiolucency in the posterior mandible. Histologically, it features islands of epithelium with peripheral cells exhibiting \"reverse polarization.\" The diagnosis is:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Odontoma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Ameloblastoma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Odontogenic Keratocyst (OKC)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Central Giant Cell Granuloma</div></div>",
