        "front": "13. A 14-year-old patient has an impacted mandibular third molar. A panoramic radiograph reveals a large, well-defined, unilocular radiolucency that attaches exactly at the cementoenamel junction (CEJ) and entirely envelops the crown of the unerupted tooth. This developmental cyst is a:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Radicular (Periapical) cyst</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Dentigerous (Follicular) cyst</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Lateral periodontal cyst</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Primordial cyst</div></div>",
