        "front": "21. A 40-year-old African American female presents for a routine panoramic radiograph. The film reveals multiple, well-defined radiopacities located at the apices of vital mandibular anterior and posterior teeth. She is completely asymptomatic. What is the diagnosis?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Condensing Osteitis</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Periapical Cemental Dysplasia</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Florid Cemento-Osseous Dysplasia</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Cementoblastoma</div></div>",
