        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "22. The Gram-negative bacterial outer membrane contains a highly toxic molecule that triggers massive inflammation, fever, and bone resorption when the bacteria die. This molecule, commonly called an \"endotoxin,\" is specifically:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Peptidoglycan</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Lipopolysaccharide (LPS)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Teichoic acid</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Hyaluronidase</div></div>",
