        "front": "25. A clinical diagnosis of \"Leukoplakia\" is strictly defined as:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> A white patch that wipes off, leaving a raw, red, bleeding surface.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> A white patch or plaque that cannot be wiped off and cannot be characterized clinically or pathologically as any other disease.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> A white lesion caused specifically by frictional trauma from a sharp tooth.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> A congenital white discoloration of the buccal mucosa that disappears when stretched.</div></div>",
