        "rationale": "Leukoplakia is a clinical \"diagnosis of exclusion.\" If a white patch doesn't wipe off (like Candida), isn't from friction (like hyperkeratosis), and isn't Lichen Planus, it is called Leukoplakia and MUST be biopsied, as it is considered potentially premalignant.",
