        "rationale": "TB triggers a Type IV Delayed Hypersensitivity reaction. The immune system cannot easily kill the waxy bacteria, so it walls them off in a \"granuloma.\" The center of this granuloma dies and rots, looking like soft white cheese (caseating necrosis).",
