        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "71. The Periodontal Ligament (PDL) has an incredibly rapid turnover rate to adapt to the constant forces of chewing and orthodontic movement. Which cell is the most abundant in the PDL and is unique because it can both synthesize AND degrade collagen?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Osteoblast</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Cementoblast</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Macrophage</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Fibroblast</div></div>",
