        "front": "82. Bacterial endospores are the most indestructible biological entities known to man, capable of surviving boiling water, radiation, and harsh chemicals. What specific chemical compound makes up 10% of the spore's weight and provides this massive resistance to heat?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Peptidoglycan</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Mycolic acid</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Calcium dipicolinate</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Lipoteichoic acid</div></div>",
