        "front": "84. Osteoradionecrosis (ORN) is a devastating complication where the jawbone dies and is exposed to the oral cavity following massive radiation therapy for head and neck cancer. According to Marx's theory, radiation causes ORN by inducing a tissue environment that is:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Hyperemic, hypercellular, and hyperoxic.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Hypovascular, hypocellular, and hypoxic.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Infected by massive bacterial invasion.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Lacking in dietary calcium.</div></div>",
