        "front": "86. Bacteria are classified by their oxygen requirements. Mycobacterium tuberculosis, the causative agent of TB, exclusively colonizes the highly oxygenated apices of the human lungs because it is an:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Obligate anaerobe</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Obligate aerobe</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Facultative anaerobe</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Microaerophile</div></div>",
