        "category": "Pathology & Microbiology",
        "front": "87. Patients suffering from Sjögren's Syndrome have a chronically hyperactive immune system attacking their salivary glands. Because of this chronic lymphocytic stimulation, these patients have a statistically massive (40x higher) risk of developing which secondary malignancy later in life?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Squamous Cell Carcinoma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Osteosarcoma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma (B-cell lymphoma)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Multiple Myeloma</div></div>",
