        "front": "3. The 'C-factor' (Configuration factor) in composite resin restorations represents the ratio of bonded to unbonded surfaces. Which of the following cavity preparations has the HIGHEST C-factor, placing the tooth at the greatest risk for polymerization shrinkage stress?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Class I</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Class II</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Class III</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Class IV</div></div>",
