        "deckName": "Day 1 Block 3: Restorative & Community Dentistry",
        "category": "Restorative & Community",
        "front": "4. In community dentistry and epidemiology, the number of NEW cases of a specific disease occurring within a defined population over a specific period of time is known as:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Prevalence</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Incidence</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Morbidity</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Mortality</div></div>",
