        "category": "Restorative & Community",
        "front": "17. A 25-year-old patient presents with a chalky white spot lesion on the facial surface of tooth #11. The surface is completely intact and hard when probed. According to the levels of prevention in public health, applying a fluoride varnish to remineralize this spot is considered:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Primary prevention</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Secondary prevention</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Tertiary prevention</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Quaternary prevention</div></div>",
