        "front": "21. A patient accidentally swallows a massive, potentially lethal dose of topical fluoride gel in the clinic. After calling emergency services, what is the immediate first-aid antidote you must administer to the patient to bind the fluoride in their stomach?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> A large glass of water</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Epinephrine</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Milk or calcium-containing antacids (e.g., Tums)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Baking soda (Sodium bicarbonate)</div></div>",
