        "front": "24. A dentist uses a 4th-generation \"total-etch\" bonding system. After etching the dentin with phosphoric acid, they accidentally dry the dentin completely with an air syringe until it is chalky white. What catastrophic restorative failure will this cause?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The composite will cure too quickly.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The collagen fibril network will collapse, preventing the resin from infiltrating and causing massive post-operative sensitivity.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The dentin will turn black.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The bonding agent will chemically dissolve the tooth.</div></div>",
