        "deckId": "day1_block3",
        "deckName": "Day 1 Block 3: Restorative & Community Dentistry",
        "category": "Restorative & Community",
        "front": "53. A randomized controlled trial (RCT) is considered the absolute gold standard of epidemiological research. What specific design feature makes an RCT superior to a cohort study?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It observes patients retrospectively.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> It eliminates random error completely.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The researcher actively controls and randomly assigns the exposure/treatment to the subjects.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> It requires thousands of more participants.</div></div>",
