        "front": "54. When preparing a Class II amalgam cavity, the axiopulpal line angle must be distinctly rounded rather than left as a sharp 90-degree corner. What is the biomechanical reason for this?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> To provide extra retention for the amalgam.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> To prevent the condensation instrument from getting stuck.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> To decrease stress concentration and prevent the amalgam from fracturing at the isthmus.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> To prevent exposing the pulp horn.</div></div>",
