        "deckName": "Day 1 Block 3: Restorative & Community Dentistry",
        "category": "Restorative & Community",
        "front": "60. The Silness-Löe Plaque Index is widely used in periodontology and public health. Unlike other indices that just look for the presence of plaque, how does the Silness-Löe index specifically score plaque?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> By weighing the plaque on a micro-scale.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> By measuring the thickness and accumulation of plaque strictly at the gingival margin.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> By observing how fast the plaque turns red when disclosing solution is applied.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> By counting the number of cavities the plaque has caused.</div></div>",
