        "category": "Restorative & Community",
        "front": "68. A 40-year-old patient comes in with intense sensitivity to cold on tooth #3. You notice severe gingival recession and a deep, V-shaped notch on the facial root surface at the CEJ. The patient has a very heavy clenching habit. This specific type of non-carious cervical lesion is termed:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Abrasion</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Attrition</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Erosion</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Abfraction</div></div>",
