        "front": "71. During the application of a dental sealant on a 6-year-old's first molar, the tooth becomes heavily contaminated with saliva right after etching. What is the absolutely mandatory clinical protocol?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Rinse the saliva, dry it, and place the sealant.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Re-etch the tooth completely for 10-15 seconds, rinse, dry, and place the sealant.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Apply a bonding agent over the saliva and cure it.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Wipe the saliva with a cotton roll and proceed.</div></div>",
