        "front": "72. Case-control studies are highly effective in epidemiology for studying rare diseases. In a case-control study, what specific statistical metric is calculated to determine the strength of the association between the exposure and the disease?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Relative Risk (RR)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Odds Ratio (OR)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Incidence Rate</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> P-value</div></div>",
