        "front": "73. A patient returns to your clinic 2 days after receiving a massive Class II amalgam restoration on tooth #30. They complain of a sharp, metallic, shock-like pain every time they close their mouth. Upon examination, you note an opposing gold crown on tooth #3. What is causing this pain?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Irreversible pulpitis</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Galvanic shock (Galvanism)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Amalgam expansion</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Secondary caries</div></div>",
