        "front": "78. In the ethical principles governing dentistry and public health, the principle of 'Beneficence' strictly demands that the dentist must:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Do no harm to the patient.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Tell the truth to the patient at all times.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Actively act in the best interest of the patient and the public to promote good.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Respect the patient's right to refuse treatment.</div></div>",
