        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "6. A patient is missing teeth #18, #19, and #20. All other mandibular teeth are present. According to the Kennedy Classification system for RPDs, this arch is classified as:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Class I</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Class II</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Class III</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Class IV</div></div>",
