        "front": "7. According to Applegate's Rules for Kennedy Classification, if a third molar is missing and will NOT be replaced with the partial denture, how does it affect the classification?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It automatically creates a Class I classification.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> It is counted as a modification space.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> It is completely ignored and not considered in the classification.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> It forces the classification to become a Class III.</div></div>",
