        "deckId": "day2_block1",
        "deckName": "Day 2 Block 1: Prosthodontics & Dental Materials",
        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "8. An irreversible hydrocolloid (Alginate) impression is highly sensitive to the environment. If an alginate impression is left sitting on the counter in the dry open air for 30 minutes, it will shrink and distort due to the evaporation of water. This specific physical process is called:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Imbibition</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Syneresis</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Hysteresis</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Polymerization</div></div>",
