        "front": "28. You are adjusting the occlusion on a new PFM crown. The porcelain is heavily scratched by your diamond bur. Which material must be used extra-orally to polish the porcelain back to a high glaze?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Pumice</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Rouge</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Diamond polishing paste</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Tin oxide</div></div>",
