        "front": "34. When selecting a shade for an all-ceramic anterior crown, the tooth must be slightly hydrated, and the dentist should glance at the shade tab for no more than 5 seconds at a time. Staring intensely at the tooth for too long will fatigue the color receptors in the eye, causing:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Metamerism</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Color adaptation (Color fatigue/Blue-Yellow blindness)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Fluorescence</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Opalescence</div></div>",
