        "front": "38. In RPD design, the \"RPI concept\" is an incredibly popular clasp assembly designed specifically for Class I and II distal extension cases to prevent torquing the abutment tooth. What do the letters R, P, and I stand for?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Rest (Mesial), Proximal Plate (Distal), I-bar (Facial)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Rest (Distal), Plate (Lingual), I-bar (Lingual)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Resin, Porcelain, Ionomer</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Rigid, Passive, Indirect</div></div>",
