        "front": "39. During the final processing of a complete denture in the lab, the acrylic resin undergoes polymerization shrinkage. Because of the physical shape of the palate, this shrinkage causes the denture base to lift away from the master cast precisely at the:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Incisive papilla</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Mid-palatal suture (center of the palate)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Posterior palatal seal</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Buccal flanges</div></div>",
