        "front": "40. Dental gypsum products (Plaster and Stone) undergo an exothermic reaction when they set. If the dental assistant mixes the stone with water that is TOO HOT (e.g., 50°C / 120°F), what will happen to the setting time?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It will drastically decrease (set too fast).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> It will drastically increase (set very slowly).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The gypsum will explode.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The water temperature has absolutely no effect.</div></div>",
