        "front": "41. You are evaluating the retention of a complete maxillary denture. The denture stays in perfectly when the patient is at rest, but instantly drops and falls down when the patient opens their mouth completely wide. What is the most likely cause?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The posterior palatal seal is too short.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The distobuccal flanges are too thick and overextended, interfering with the coronoid process.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The VDO is too large.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The teeth are set in crossbite.</div></div>",
