        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "42. According to the mechanics of fixed partial dentures (bridges), Ante's Law is a golden mathematical rule that must be obeyed to ensure the bridge does not fail under chewing forces. What does Ante's Law state?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The pontic must be narrower than the abutments.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The combined root surface area of all abutment teeth must be equal to or greater than the root surface area of the teeth being replaced.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The bridge must not span more than two teeth.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The ferrule must be 2mm.</div></div>",
