        "front": "46. A 10-year-old child completely avulses (knocks out) tooth #8. The mother calls you in a panic. You instruct her to gently rinse the tooth without touching the root and immediately place it in a transport medium to keep the PDL cells alive. Which liquid is considered the BEST transport medium?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Cold tap water</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Saliva (spitting in a cup)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Cold milk or Hank's Balanced Salt Solution (HBSS)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Rubbing alcohol</div></div>",
