        "front": "48. During the fabrication of a metal-ceramic (PFM) crown, the metal substructure goes through an 'oxidizing' or 'degassing' cycle in the oven before the porcelain is applied. What is the purpose of this crucial step?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> To melt the metal to fit the die.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> To completely sterilize the metal.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> To form a microscopic oxide layer on the metal surface, which is absolutely required for the porcelain to chemically bond to the metal.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> To make the metal look tooth-colored.</div></div>",
