        "front": "52. When mixing Alginate (irreversible hydrocolloid), the assistant uses water that is significantly colder than room temperature. What effect will this have on the material?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It will completely prevent the alginate from setting.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> It will significantly increase (lengthen) the setting time, giving the operator more working time.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> It will decrease the setting time, making it set instantly.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> It will cause the alginate to become rock hard and impossible to remove.</div></div>",
