        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "68. Which type of dental cement is renowned for causing the LEAST amount of pulpal irritation, making it the safest choice for cementing a crown on a tooth with a very deep preparation and a hyperemic pulp?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Zinc phosphate</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Glass ionomer</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Resin cement</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Zinc oxide eugenol (ZOE) or Polycarboxylate</div></div>",
