        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "69. You are surveying a master cast for an RPD. You find an undercut on the abutment tooth that measures exactly 0.01 inches (0.25 mm). Which type of clasp material is strictly indicated for engaging this specific depth of undercut?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Cast Cobalt-Chromium (Co-Cr)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Wrought wire</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Cast Gold</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Titanium alloy</div></div>",
