        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "71. During the fabrication of a metal-ceramic (PFM) restoration, what is the primary function of the 'opaque' layer of porcelain?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> To provide the final shiny glaze.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> To physically mask the dark color of the metal oxide layer and initiate the chemical bond to the metal.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> To simulate the translucency of natural enamel.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> To prevent the metal from rusting.</div></div>",
