        "deckName": "Day 2 Block 1: Prosthodontics & Dental Materials",
        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "72. You are preparing an anterior tooth for a full-coverage crown. Why is it absolutely contraindicated to create a 'feather-edge' margin preparation for an all-ceramic or PFM crown?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It requires removing too much tooth structure.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> It does not provide enough bulk/thickness at the margin, causing the brittle porcelain to easily fracture.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> It is too difficult for the lab to see.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> It will cause hypercementosis.</div></div>",
