        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "77. Dental ceramics (porcelains) are highly esthetic but incredibly brittle. To prevent catastrophic failure, a PFM crown is designed so that the porcelain is placed under which specific type of stress?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Tensile stress</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Compressive stress</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Shear stress</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Torsional stress</div></div>",
