        "front": "80. When recording Centric Relation (CR) for a totally edentulous patient, it is crucial to understand the anatomy of the jaw joint. Centric Relation is defined as the position where the condyles are located in the:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Most anterior-superior position against the articular eminences.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Most posterior-inferior position in the glenoid fossa.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Most lateral border position.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Maximum intercuspal position.</div></div>",
