        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "88. A patient complains that their upper complete denture drops down every time they smile widely or yawn. Upon examination, the denture fits perfectly at rest. What is the most likely error?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The posterior palatal seal is missing.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The buccal notches for the buccal frenum are too narrow/shallow, or the buccal flanges are too thick.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The teeth are set too far lingually.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The patient has no saliva.</div></div>",
