        "front": "89. Glass ionomer cements undergo an acid-base reaction. During the very early stages of setting, the cement is highly vulnerable to moisture contamination because which specific ion has not yet cross-linked the matrix?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Calcium</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Aluminum</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Fluoride</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Sodium</div></div>",
