        "id": "deck-day2_block1-098",
        "deckId": "day2_block1",
        "deckName": "Day 2 Block 1: Prosthodontics & Dental Materials",
        "category": "Prostho & Materials",
        "front": "98. In the preparation of a post space for a root-canal treated tooth, maintaining the apical seal is the highest priority. What is the absolute minimum amount of gutta-percha that MUST be left intact at the apex of the root to prevent bacterial leakage?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> 1.0 to 2.0 mm</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> 3.0 to 5.0 mm</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> 7.0 mm</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> None, the post should reach the absolute tip.</div></div>",
