        "category": "Roentgenology & Surgery",
        "front": "2. You are preparing to extract tooth #30 (a mandibular first molar) that has severely decayed, bifurcated roots. Which specific extraction forceps is uniquely designed with paired, pointed beaks (the 'cowhorn') to slide perfectly into the root bifurcation of lower molars?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Forceps #150</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Forceps #151</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Forceps #23</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Forceps #88R</div></div>",
