        "front": "10. Which physical component of the x-ray tubehead is made of aluminum and functions specifically to absorb the low-energy, long-wavelength x-ray photons that only harm the patient without contributing to the image?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The collimator</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The filter</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The tungsten filament</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The focusing cup</div></div>",
