        "deckName": "Day 2 Block 2: Roentgenology, Diagnosis & Oral Surgery",
        "category": "Roentgenology & Surgery",
        "front": "12. In the event of a severe allergic reaction (Anaphylaxis) in the dental chair, what is the single most important, life-saving drug that must be administered immediately?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Diphenhydramine (Benadryl)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Albuterol</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Epinephrine (Adrenaline) 1:1,000</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Nitroglycerin</div></div>",
