        "front": "14. A patient taking Warfarin (Coumadin) needs an extraction. You must request their INR (International Normalized Ratio) blood test results before proceeding. For a routine, non-surgical extraction, what is the maximum acceptable INR level to safely proceed without adjusting their medication?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> 1.0</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> 2.5 to 3.0</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> 5.0</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> 10.0</div></div>",
