        "deckName": "Day 2 Block 2: Roentgenology, Diagnosis & Oral Surgery",
        "category": "Roentgenology & Surgery",
        "front": "22. The Inverse Square Law is a critical principle in radiation physics. If you double the distance between the x-ray tubehead and the patient (e.g., moving from an 8-inch PID to a 16-inch PID), how is the intensity of the x-ray beam affected?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The intensity is reduced to 1/2 of its original power.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The intensity is reduced to 1/4 of its original power.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The intensity is doubled.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The intensity is squared.</div></div>",
