        "front": "28. When evaluating a panoramic radiograph, you notice a massive, ghost-like radiopaque shadow draped straight across the anterior teeth, obscuring the apices of the maxillary incisors. What technical error caused this?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The patient's chin was tilted too far down.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The patient was slumped over, creating a shadow of their cervical spine (neck).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The patient failed to place their tongue flat against the roof of their mouth.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The patient was wearing a thyroid collar.</div></div>",
