        "front": "31. Following a traumatic injury to the face, a patient complains that their teeth no longer fit together correctly. You suspect a mandibular fracture. Statistically, what is the single most common location for a fracture of the mandible?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The symphysis (midline)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The angle of the mandible</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The body of the mandible</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The condyle</div></div>",
