        "category": "Roentgenology & Surgery",
        "front": "37. During the extraction of an upper first molar, a distinct 'hollow' popping sound is heard, and the patient complains that air is rushing into their mouth when they breathe through their nose. You have created an Oroantral Communication (OAC). If the hole is 4 millimeters wide, what is the proper treatment?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Do nothing, it will heal normally.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Pack the socket entirely with Gelfoam and suture a figure-eight over the socket, placing the patient on sinus precautions.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Immediately perform a buccal advancement flap to drag tissue over the hole and seal it completely.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Prescribe nasal spray and wait 3 months.</div></div>",
