        "front": "45. Le Fort fractures are devastating facial traumas resulting from massive blunt force (like car accidents). A Le Fort II fracture specifically describes a fracture line that separates:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The maxilla straight across horizontally above the teeth (floating palate).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The maxilla and the nasal bones from the rest of the face, creating a pyramid shape (pyramidal fracture).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The entire facial skeleton from the cranial base (craniofacial disjunction).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The mandible at the symphysis.</div></div>",
