        "answer": "Correct Answer: B. Do not stop the Aspirin; proceed with the extraction and use local hemostatic measures.",
        "rationale": "Low-dose aspirin (81mg) permanently disables platelets, but modern standards dictate you NEVER take a patient off their daily Aspirin for routine dental surgery. The risk of them having a fatal heart attack or stroke far outweighs the risk of the socket bleeding slightly more than normal.",
        "type": "prc-block"
