        "deckId": "day2_block2",
        "deckName": "Day 2 Block 2: Roentgenology, Diagnosis & Oral Surgery",
        "category": "Roentgenology & Surgery",
        "front": "82. You are using an elevator to luxate a difficult tooth. To prevent accidentally breaking the patient's jaw or crushing adjacent teeth, you must NEVER use which anatomical structure as a fulcrum?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The crestal alveolar bone</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The adjacent natural tooth</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The root of the tooth being extracted</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The interseptal bone</div></div>",
