        "category": "Roentgenology & Surgery",
        "front": "87. You take a bitewing radiograph and notice that the image appears 'foggy', gray, and lacks sharp contrast. What is the most common darkroom error that causes film fog?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> A light leak in the darkroom or an improper safelight.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The developer was too cold.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The patient moved.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The film was placed backwards in the mouth.</div></div>",
