        "front": "88. A patient is scheduled for orthognathic surgery to fix a severe underbite. The surgeon will perform a Bilateral Sagittal Split Osteotomy (BSSO) to slide the entire lower jaw forward. What is the most frequent, severe post-operative complication of a BSSO?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Fracture of the maxilla.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Temporary or permanent numbness (paresthesia) of the lower lip and chin.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Blindness.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Total loss of the tongue.</div></div>",
