        "front": "91. A patient presents with a severe, throbbing toothache that wakes them up at night. However, when you test the tooth with Endo-Ice (cold test), they feel absolutely nothing. What does this indicate?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The pulp is perfectly healthy.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The patient is faking the pain.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The pulp is completely necrotic (dead).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The patient has reversible pulpitis.</div></div>",
