        "front": "93. A pediatric patient presents with severe delayed eruption of all permanent teeth. Upon radiographic examination, you notice the patient completely lacks clavicles (collarbones) and has dozens of supernumerary, impacted teeth trapped in their jaws. What is the diagnosis?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Down Syndrome</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Cleidocranial Dysplasia</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Gardner Syndrome</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Ectodermal Dysplasia</div></div>",
