        "deckId": "day2_block2",
        "deckName": "Day 2 Block 2: Roentgenology, Diagnosis & Oral Surgery",
        "category": "Roentgenology & Surgery",
        "front": "94. You are performing an apicoectomy (root-end surgery) on tooth #8 because a previous root canal failed. After cutting off the tip of the infected root and cleaning the bone, what is the 'gold standard' material used to seal the retro-preparation at the apex of the root?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Amalgam</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Composite resin</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Mineral Trioxide Aggregate (MTA)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Gutta-percha</div></div>",
