        "front": "97. A patient presents with a severe infection of the maxillary canine (tooth #6). Because the root of the canine is so incredibly long, the infection frequently breaks through the bone ABOVE the attachment of the levator anguli oris muscle. This dumps the pus directly into which space, causing massive swelling under the eye?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Buccal space</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Canine space</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Infratemporal space</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Submandibular space</div></div>",
