        "category": "Anesthesia & Pharmacology",
        "front": "1. Local anesthetics are chemically classified as either amides or esters. Which of the following is the primary site of biotransformation (metabolism) for AMIDE local anesthetics?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Blood plasma</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Kidneys</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Liver</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Lungs</div></div>",
