        "rationale": "Local anesthetics are base molecules. The un-ionized base crosses the lipid membrane into the nerve cell, converts to an ionized acid, and physically plugs the voltage-gated sodium channel from the INSIDE, stopping sodium from rushing in and firing the nerve.",
