        "category": "Anesthesia & Pharmacology",
        "front": "30. Acyclovir is the primary antiviral medication prescribed for severe Herpes Simplex (HSV) infections. What is its specific mechanism of action?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It destroys the viral envelope.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> It acts as a fake DNA building block, completely inhibiting viral DNA polymerase and stopping viral replication.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> It physically blocks the virus from entering the host cell.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> It triggers the host cell to commit apoptosis.</div></div>",
