        "front": "35. Benzodiazepines (like Diazepam and Midazolam) are the most frequently prescribed oral sedatives in dentistry to reduce patient anxiety. What is their mechanism of action?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> They block serotonin reuptake.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> They bind to the GABA-A receptor, increasing the FREQUENCY of chloride channel openings, heavily depressing the central nervous system.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> They act as direct dopamine agonists.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> They destroy the amygdala.</div></div>",
