        "front": "41. When prescribing a drug, the 'Therapeutic Index' (TI) is the ratio of the Lethal Dose (LD50) to the Effective Dose (ED50). Clinically, a drug with a very NARROW (small) therapeutic index means:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It is incredibly safe and virtually impossible to overdose on.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The dose that cures the patient is terrifyingly close to the dose that kills the patient, requiring extreme caution and constant blood monitoring.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The drug only works on a narrow range of bacteria.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The drug is available over-the-counter.</div></div>",
