        "front": "42. Corticosteroids (like Prednisone or Dexamethasone) are the absolute most powerful anti-inflammatory drugs in medicine. How do they shut down massive inflammation and swelling?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> They block COX-1 entirely.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> They block Phospholipase A2, completely shutting down the release of arachidonic acid, thereby stopping the production of BOTH prostaglandins and leukotrienes.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> They kill white blood cells.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> They act as an antihistamine.</div></div>",
