        "front": "54. Mepivacaine 3% plain (Carbocaine without vasoconstrictor) is frequently selected when a vasoconstrictor is contraindicated. Why does Mepivacaine produce acceptable pulpal anesthesia even without epinephrine?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> It has the lowest pKa of all amides.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> It produces the least amount of vasodilation of all standard dental amide anesthetics.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> It is metabolized in the blood plasma.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> It is naturally an intense vasoconstrictor.</div></div>",
