        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 1: Pediatric Dentistry & Orthodontics",
        "category": "Pediatric & Orthodontics",
        "front": "24. A child presents with a \"Distal Step\" relationship in their primary molars (the lower primary 2nd molar is situated significantly farther back than the upper). What will this inevitably develop into in the permanent dentition?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Angle Class I</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Angle Class II</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Angle Class III</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Anterior crossbite</div></div>",
