        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 1: Pediatric Dentistry & Orthodontics",
        "category": "Pediatric & Orthodontics",
        "front": "26. When evaluating the growth of the human skull, the bones of the cranial vault (the flat bones covering the brain) grow via which biological process?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Endochondral ossification</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Intramembranous ossification</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Sutural expansion only</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Appositional cartilage growth</div></div>",
