        "deckId": "day3_block1",
        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 1: Pediatric Dentistry & Orthodontics",
        "category": "Pediatric & Orthodontics",
        "front": "27. In the analysis of a mixed dentition arch, the Bolton Analysis is specifically used mathematically to determine:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> If there is enough space in the arch for the unerupted premolars.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> If there is a Tooth Size Discrepancy (TSD) between the size of the upper teeth and the size of the lower teeth.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The skeletal angle of the mandible.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The exact size of the leeway space.</div></div>",
