        "front": "30. To break a severe thumb-sucking or tongue-thrusting habit in an older child, a fixed appliance can be cemented to the maxillary molars with a wire cage resting behind the front teeth. This appliance is called a:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Lip bumper</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Palatal crib (Habit crib)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Pendulum appliance</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Quad helix</div></div>",
