        "front": "39. Which genetic disorder is characterized by a high risk of periodontal disease, a massive, fissured, protruding tongue (macroglossia), delayed eruption of teeth, and a statistically lower risk of dental caries?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Ectodermal Dysplasia</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Down Syndrome (Trisomy 21)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Cleidocranial Dysplasia</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Crouzon Syndrome</div></div>",
