        "front": "51. In pediatric endodontics, a pulpectomy is performed on a primary tooth with irreversible pulpitis. Which of the following materials is strictly CONTRAINDICATED for obturating (filling) the root canals of a primary tooth?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Zinc Oxide Eugenol (ZOE) paste</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Iodoform-based paste (e.g., Vitapex)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Calcium hydroxide paste</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Gutta-percha</div></div>",
