        "deckId": "day3_block2",
        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 2: Dental Jurisprudence, Ethics & Practice",
        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "5. In the ethical principles of dentistry, the concept of 'Autonomy' dictates that the dentist must:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Do absolutely no harm to the patient.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Provide the highest standard of care to everyone equally.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Respect the patient's right to self-determination and allow them to make their own informed decisions regarding their treatment.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Tell the truth to the patient at all times.</div></div>",
