        "id": "deck-day3_block2-006",
        "deckId": "day3_block2",
        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 2: Dental Jurisprudence, Ethics & Practice",
        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "6. A patient sits in the dental chair, opens their mouth, and allows the dentist to examine their teeth with a mirror and explorer without signing a piece of paper. In legal terms, the patient has just provided:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Expressed consent</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Implied consent</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Informed consent</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Proxy consent</div></div>",
