        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "9. A court issues a legal order demanding that a dentist physically bring a specific patient's dental records, x-rays, and study casts to the courtroom for a trial. This specific legal document is called a:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Subpoena ad testificandum</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Subpoena duces tecum</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Writ of Mandamus</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Summons</div></div>",
