        "front": "12. In writing a prescription, the section that contains the actual name of the drug, the dosage (e.g., Amoxicillin 500mg), and the quantity to be dispensed is called the:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Superscription</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Inscription</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Subscription</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Signatura</div></div>",
