        "front": "14. A patient fails to follow the dentist's strict post-operative instructions after a surgical extraction (e.g., they smoked and rigorously rinsed their mouth), leading to a massive infection and hospitalization. If the patient sues the dentist, the dentist can use which legal defense?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Res ipsa loquitur</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Contributory negligence</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Statute of frauds</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Ignorantia juris</div></div>",
