        "front": "19. The concept of 'Four-Handed Dentistry' revolutionized clinical practice management and ergonomics. What is the primary objective of four-handed dentistry?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> To allow the dentist to work standing up.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> To double the clinical fees charged to the patient.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> To increase efficiency, minimize stress and fatigue on the dental team, and keep the dentist's eyes focused continuously on the operative field.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> To eliminate the need for high-volume suction.</div></div>",
