        "front": "20. In dental ergonomics, the operatory is divided into 'Zones of Activity' around the patient's head (imagined as a clock face). For a right-handed dentist, the 'Transfer Zone' where instruments and materials are safely passed is located at:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> 12 o'clock to 2 o'clock</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> 2 o'clock to 4 o'clock</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> 4 o'clock to 7 o'clock</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> 7 o'clock to 12 o'clock</div></div>",
