        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "30. The Data Privacy Act of 2012 (R.A. 10173) heavily impacts dental practice management. Under this law, what is the dentist's legal obligation regarding patient records?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> They must publish the names of patients who owe money.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> They must implement strict security measures to protect the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of patients' personal and sensitive health information.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> They must share all records with the PDA.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> They can sell patient contact info to toothbrush companies.</div></div>",
