        "front": "35. If a dentist decides to end the dentist-patient relationship (dismiss the patient) because the patient is highly abusive and refuses to pay, the dentist MUST follow proper protocol. If the dentist just stops treating the patient midway through a root canal without notice, the dentist is guilty of:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Assault</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Battery</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Abandonment</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Contributory negligence</div></div>",
