        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "36. In a civil malpractice suit, the patient (plaintiff) must prove four elements to win the case: Duty, Dereliction (Breach of duty), Direct Causation, and:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Damages (actual injury or harm)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Death</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Defamation</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Deductibles</div></div>",
