        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "45. You are the only dentist in a small rural town. An individual walks into your clinic suffering from life-threatening massive bleeding after a car accident. Ethically and legally, what is your duty?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Refuse to see them because they don't have an appointment.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Refuse to see them because trauma is not a dental issue.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> You have a duty to render emergency first aid to the best of your ability to save their life, even if it is outside your normal scope, until medical help arrives.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Ask for their insurance card first.</div></div>",
