        "front": "49. In marketing a dental practice, 'Internal Marketing' refers to:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Buying billboards on the highway.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Running Facebook and Google Ads.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Strategies directed at existing patients to encourage retention and referrals (e.g., sending birthday cards, making post-op phone calls, providing excellent customer service).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Handing out flyers at the mall.</div></div>",
