        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "59. In the business structure of a dental practice, a 'Sole Proprietorship' is the most common format. What is the greatest financial disadvantage of operating as a Sole Proprietor?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> You have to split the profits with a partner.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Unlimited personal liability (if the clinic is sued and goes bankrupt, the court can seize your personal house and car to pay the clinic's debts).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> You cannot hire any employees.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> You pay double the taxes.</div></div>",
