        "front": "71. In dental ergonomics, avoiding twisting your torso and reaching violently behind your back is crucial for a long career. A motion that involves twisting the torso and reaching with the entire arm is classified as a:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Class II motion</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Class III motion</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Class IV motion</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Class V motion</div></div>",
