        "category": "Jurisprudence & Ethics",
        "front": "72. If a dentist promises a patient, 'I guarantee this set of veneers will make you look exactly like a movie star,' but the patient is unhappy with the result, the dentist can be successfully sued for:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Malpractice (Negligence)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Breach of Contract</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Assault</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Defamation</div></div>",
