        "front": "79. The principle of 'Comparative Negligence' is used in civil court to determine damages. What does it mean?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The dentist is 100% at fault.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The damages awarded are reduced by the percentage of fault attributed to the patient (e.g., if the patient was 20% at fault for ignoring instructions, the dentist only pays 80% of the damages).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The patient gets double the money.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The dentist goes to jail.</div></div>",
