        "rationale": "A natural tooth is suspended in a shock-absorbing hammock (the PDL). An implant is fused directly to solid bone (osseointegration). Because it lacks a PDL and perpendicular inserting fibers, an implant has zero shock absorption and relies on a fragile 'O-ring' of parallel fibers to keep bacteria out.",
        "type": "prc-block"
