        "front": "24. C-shaped root canals are a complex, treacherous anatomical variation where the mesial and distal canals fuse into a massive 'C' ribbon. In which specific tooth are C-shaped canals statistically most common, particularly in Asian populations?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Maxillary first molar</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Mandibular first molar</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Mandibular second molar</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Maxillary first premolar</div></div>",
