        "deckId": "day3_block3",
        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 3: Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "25. A patient undergoes a Free Gingival Graft (FGG) procedure, where a piece of tissue is cut from their palate and sutured to their lower anterior gums. What is the absolute primary clinical objective of performing an FGG?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> To cover exposed, sensitive roots (Root coverage).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> To increase the width and thickness of the tough, keratinized Attached Gingiva.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> To regenerate alveolar bone.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> To cure gingivitis.</div></div>",
