        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 3: Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "32. In a failed root canal retreatment case, the canal is often heavily contaminated by a highly resistant, Gram-positive facultative anaerobic bacteria that can survive starvation and harsh chemicals (like Calcium Hydroxide). What is this notorious endodontic pathogen?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Streptococcus mutans</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Porphyromonas gingivalis</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Enterococcus faecalis</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Actinomyces israelii</div></div>",
