        "rationale": "Gates Glidden drills look like little footballs on a long latch-grip shank. They are used purely to open, flare, and move the orifice of the canal in the top 1/3 of the root to achieve straight-line access. Pushing them deep into a canal will instantly cause a lateral perforation.",
