        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "38. You are attempting to negotiate a calcified root canal using a size 10 file. To aid in slipping the file down the tight canal, you use a thick, paste-like lubricant (like RC-Prep). What is the primary active chemical in these endodontic lubricants?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Eugenol</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> EDTA</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Sodium hypochlorite</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Calcium hydroxide</div></div>",
