        "front": "39. During a periodontal exam, you notice that tooth #8 has 2 millimeters of visible recession, but the pocket depth is only 1 millimeter. The tooth moves more than 1 millimeter horizontally when pushed, but cannot be depressed vertically. What is its Miller Mobility score?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Class 1</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Class 2</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Class 3</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Class 4</div></div>",
