        "deckId": "day3_block3",
        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 3: Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "43. In periodontal disease, massive alveolar bone destruction is driven by the patient's own immune system overreacting to the bacteria. Which specific host-derived cytokine is considered the most potent stimulator of osteoclast activation and bone resorption?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Interleukin-1 (IL-1)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Histamine</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> IgG antibodies</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Amylase</div></div>",
