        "front": "58. Gutta-percha relies on endodontic sealer to create a fluid-tight seal. Which of the following is the primary, most crucial biological function of the root canal sealer?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> To physically strengthen the root to prevent fracture.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> To fill the microscopic voids, lateral canals, and gaps between the gutta-percha and the dentin walls that the solid rubber cones cannot reach.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> To release fluoride and remineralize the root.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> To bleach the tooth white.</div></div>",
