        "front": "61. Guided Tissue Regeneration (GTR) uses barrier membranes and bone grafts to regrow lost attachment. Mathematically, which specific type of bone defect has the absolute HIGHEST predictability and success rate for GTR?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> A 1-wall defect (Hemiseptal defect).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> A 2-wall defect (Crater).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> A deep, narrow 3-wall intrabony defect (Trough).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Horizontal bone loss.</div></div>",
