        "front": "64. In endodontic pathology, Apical Periodontitis is defined as the inflammatory destruction of the bone around the apex of a tooth. What is the definitive, overwhelmingly primary cause of apical periodontitis?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Occlusal trauma from a high filling.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Bacterial invasion and colonization of the necrotic pulp space.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Systemic immune deficiency.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> An allergic reaction to gutta-percha.</div></div>",
