        "front": "68. A patient is in a car accident and sustains a Horizontal Root Fracture in the middle third of tooth #8. The tooth is heavily displaced backward. You instantly reposition it. According to the IADT trauma guidelines, how long must this horizontal root fracture be splinted with a flexible wire?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> 1 week</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> 2 weeks</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> 4 weeks</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> 4 months</div></div>",
