        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "69. You perform comprehensive Scaling and Root Planing (Phase I Therapy) on a patient with severe periodontitis. The gums are bleeding heavily. To accurately assess the healing, pocket reduction, and need for surgery, you must schedule a re-evaluation appointment. How long must you wait?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> 1 week</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> 4 to 6 weeks</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> 3 months</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> 6 months</div></div>",
