        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "70. A tooth suffers from a 'True Combined Endo-Perio Lesion,' where a severe apical endodontic abscess has met and joined together with a deep periodontal pocket, forming one massive defect. What is the mandatory sequence of treatment?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Extract the tooth instantly.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Perform Periodontal surgery first, then do the Root Canal.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Perform the Root Canal (Endodontic therapy) first, wait for it to heal, and then evaluate the need for Periodontal therapy.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Prescribe antibiotics and do both at the exact same time.</div></div>",
