        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 3: Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "72. When preparing the mesial root of a mandibular first molar, the dentist must be extremely cautious of the 'Danger Zone'. Over-filing this area will cause a catastrophic 'strip perforation'. Where exactly is this danger zone located?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The buccal wall of the mesial root.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The distal aspect (the furcation side) of the mesial root.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The mesial aspect of the mesial root.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The lingual wall of the distal root.</div></div>",
