        "deckName": "Day 3 Block 3: Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "73. Modern periodontology relies on the 'Host-Bacterial Interaction' theory. While bacteria initiate the disease, what specifically causes the vast majority of the actual tissue and bone destruction in periodontitis?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> The bacteria physically eating the bone.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> The highly acidic bacterial waste products dissolving the bone.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> The host's own hyperactive immune response (Neutrophils and Macrophages releasing MMPs and Cytokines) destroying the tissue in an attempt to fight the bacteria.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> The forceful trauma of toothbrushing.</div></div>",
