        "front": "75. A patient suffering from severe Vitamin C deficiency (Scurvy) presents with violently bleeding, swollen, and spontaneously falling-out teeth. Vitamin C is biologically essential for the synthesis of what major structural component of the periodontium?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Elastin</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Collagen (specifically the hydroxylation of proline and lysine)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Hydroxyapatite</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Keratin</div></div>",
