        "front": "76. You finish a root canal on tooth #8. The post-operative radiograph shows the gutta-percha filling looks perfectly dense, but the cone was shoved 3 millimeters OUT of the root apex into the surrounding jawbone. This specific procedural error is defined as:<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> Overfilling</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> Overextension</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> Underfilling</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> Zipping</div></div>",
