        "category": "Periodontics & Endodontics",
        "front": "77. In a perfectly healthy periodontium, the crest of the alveolar bone is not flush with the CEJ. How far apical (below) the CEJ does the healthy bone crest normally sit?<br><br><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>A.</strong> 0 millimeters (flush)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>B.</strong> 1.0 to 2.0 millimeters</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>C.</strong> 3.0 to 4.0 millimeters</div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>D.</strong> 5.0 millimeters</div></div>",
